{"kind":"report","text":"Exact-head review of 45c7946ffd53de2d9ee3021c9e32924ec3c24586, resting on all 60 artifacts, primary packages/room/README.md first. Changes requested.\n\nArchitecture: phase 2b is a substantial improvement. Landing, workspaces, pinning, tree differences and log publication now use the real B/L engines on the Room's SQLite; only the remote transport is fake in the acceptance suite. The reservation, unknown-push, abort, lease-race, scoped-input and offline replay cases give meaningful integration evidence. All packages/git and packages/log blobs match the approved B6/L4 heads. The outstanding work below remains part of the complete scope.\n\n1. P1: stored check carries bypass a later policy that disables or refuses carry (core.ts activate/carryChecks; obligations.ts obligationStatus; store.ts check_carries). Carry rows have no policy-version binding and activation never invalidates them. The calculator accepts those rows using only checker configuration/authority/validity; carryChecks returns early when carry.checks is false or a carry rule exists, leaving prior rows eligible. Independent real-SQLite reproductions hold an unreserved operation ready after a scoped carry, activate either carry.checks:false or a check carry rule with allow:\"false\", run recompute/readiness/reservation, and still land. Invalidate/rejudge carries on activation and bind persisted judgments to the exact active policy and integration. Both forms must leave the obligation open and prevent reservation; changing checker configuration/global inputs and retirement/compromise should remain covered.\n\n2. P2: migration discards outstanding workspace cleanup (store.ts migration 6; core.ts endedWorkspaces/revokeEndedTokens). Every previous workspace becomes ws_leases.state='ended' before its access has been revoked; the old fork_tokens IDs are no longer consumed. An older ready workspace with a live 30-minute write token is migrated, then released: three alarm runs leave the token live and Workspaces.pendingCleanup() is zero. A holder reopening someday is not cleanup of an ended lease. Import existing access and provisioning uncertainty into durable cleanup duties, retain them across failures/restarts, and mark access ended only according to its real cleanup state. Test release, expiry and take-over without any reopening.\n\n3. P2: a previously founded Room cannot use the new landing publisher (core.ts constructor/found, canonical_remote). Only a new founding stores canonical_remote; older founded stores lack it and the publisher receives an empty remote. Re-founding returns the existing Room without filling it. Independent reproduction removes the field that the old schema never had, evicts the instance, admits a new land and runs three alarms: no push is made and it never lands. Resolve and persist the exact bound canonical repository's remote during upgrade/reopening before publisher work; keep outages retryable and prevent identity substitution.\n\n4. P1.9 remains open for full integration, with credit for the work above. This head's production log push and merged preview integration are explicitly unavailable; B follow-up 855927cf now supplies a candidate that A must adopt after its own review. Check carry also needs a prospective runner/environment digest: setting facts.now.runner to the earlier check's runner makes the R-CARRY-6 comparison tautological. Fail closed until the current environment is attested/pinned. Implement and seal applicable policy carry decisions rather than permanently disabling check carry whenever any carry rule exists. Complete real A/G scoped job flow: the contract's CheckJob.integration is the filtered snapshot commit and G signs that value, whereas A accepts only its canonical preview/landing integration. A contract-shaped scoped check with the right snapshot is independently refused with check-binding. Resolve the commit identities explicitly and test the actual checker service through Room admission. Also reconcile the signed check's volatile flag with the configured flag: the current boundary accepts and carries a body declaring volatile:true under a volatile:false configuration. This is a demonstrated cross-lane inconsistency, not a claim that R-CARRY-10 already specifies which inconsistent value wins. Reject inconsistent attestations or adopt the conservative explicit contract. Keep every section 23 case covered and distinguish local/fake evidence from deployment measurements.\n\nSecurity: canonical publication credentials stay outside proposal execution, and the new guards and offline verification are valuable. Policy carry invalidation and inherited credential cleanup must be corrected; the scoped job and runner binding gaps must not silently weaken evidence reuse.\n\nSimplification: removing the Room's duplicate landing/log/verifier implementations is the right direction. Use one durable model for old and new cleanup, and policy-bound carry judgments consumed by the one obligation calculator.\n\nValidation: clean root strict type check; 65 Node and 237 workerd baseline tests passed. Six independent workerd/SQLite diagnostic cases passed while asserting the failures described above (two policy invalidation cases, inherited token cleanup, missing canonical remote, volatile mismatch and scoped snapshot commit admission). Diagnostic file is /tmp/artroom-checker-A5-diagnostics/checker-phase2b-review.test.ts; copy it beside phase2b.test.ts in this isolated candidate to rerun it. It was removed from the candidate after running; git status is clean. 27 Room artifacts are byte-identical to A4; all 32 changed current Room artifacts and the three deletions were reviewed, plus package-lock.json. All 43 inherited changed lock descriptors match approved B6; the remaining changed descriptor only adds the Room's B/L workspace dependencies. No live deployment or measurement driver was run.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0be8b7f7d5282de7d356d91517c7dbfb20700802","binding":"assigned","head":"45c7946ffd53de2d9ee3021c9e32924ec3c24586","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8f3895af927688e4f10848ebacc836dacae27ea6\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d2409eaede0361d81de52cb482c667967a64779c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eded18a4faa6fc6eafac360959e07ef5f883fa9b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}